power: supply: UMP9620 fuel gauge and bq2560x charger only on a board with a battery (F50, V50: none)

Ported from kanoqwq/mu300-linux f59a2968 (his patch 0019, "isolate UMP9620 battery drivers before register access").

The F50 and the V50 share the U30 Air's PMIC and ZTE's charger node but have no battery. Under mainline the
UMP9620's fuel gauge still bound there and listed a "Battery" (sc27xx-fgu) with made-up readings: status Full, health
"Over voltage", a temperature from an unconnected NTC input. mu300-power, mu300-api, the panel, thermal-guard,
mu300-sms-forward and the LuCI dashboard each had to be told by the board to ignore it. Patch 0016 already keeps the
charger's 0x1a fallback to the board with a battery; the charger at the node's own address stayed reachable.

Both probes now end with -ENODEV before any register access unless the device tree has the U30 Air's charger policy
service: the same test as patch 0016, patch 0023 and mu300-device (kano's version also asks of_device_is_available;
the node is only ever tested for presence here, so a U30 Air is told apart exactly as everywhere else). Only the
UMP9620 gauge ("sprd,ump9620-fgu") and ZTE's charger node ("ti,bq2560x_chg") are affected; other SC27xx and BQ256xx
boards keep their behaviour.

--- a/drivers/power/supply/bq256xx_charger.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/bq256xx_charger.c
@@ -2289,7 +2289,21 @@
 	struct i2c_client *chip = client;	/* where the registers are: 0x1a for the SGM41513 */
 
 	int ret;
+
+	/*
+	 * MU300 (kanoqwq f59a2968): ZTE's charger node is on every board of this family, but there is a battery to
+	 * charge only where the device tree has the U30 Air's charger policy service (the test of patch 0016 and
+	 * mu300-device). The F50 and V50 have none: no register of either charger address is touched there, so no
+	 * chip that answers at the node's own address can be set up to charge a battery that is not there.
+	 */
+	if (of_device_is_compatible(dev->of_node, "ti,bq2560x_chg")) {
+		struct device_node *policy = of_find_node_by_path("/charger_policy_service");
 
+		of_node_put(policy);
+		if (!policy)
+			return -ENODEV;
+	}
+
 	bq = devm_kzalloc(dev, sizeof(*bq), GFP_KERNEL);
 	if (!bq)
 		return -ENOMEM;
--- a/drivers/power/supply/sc27xx_fuel_gauge.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/sc27xx_fuel_gauge.c
@@ -1405,6 +1405,19 @@
 	struct sc27xx_fgu_data *data;
 	int ret, irq;
 
+	/*
+	 * MU300 (kanoqwq f59a2968): the F50 and V50 have the UMP9620's fuel gauge but no battery; bound, it reported
+	 * one with made-up readings (19 %, "Over voltage", 75 C from an unconnected NTC) that every user-space reader
+	 * had to be told to ignore. Only the U30 Air's device tree has the charger policy service.
+	 */
+	if (of_device_is_compatible(dev->of_node, "sprd,ump9620-fgu")) {
+		struct device_node *policy = of_find_node_by_path("/charger_policy_service");
+
+		of_node_put(policy);
+		if (!policy)
+			return -ENODEV;
+	}
+
 	data = devm_kzalloc(dev, sizeof(*data), GFP_KERNEL);
 	if (!data)
 		return -ENOMEM;
